//- Glossary. Params: d.
div(data-ui="prose")
  dl
    dt#anchor Anchor
    dd An item's start, a keyframe or a marker pinned to a word of the narration, so it stays on that word when the take changes.
    dt#asset Asset
    dd
      raw md("A reusable building block in the library: a function that draws, returns a value, makes sound, moves, transitions or processes pixels, or a file (picture, sound, font, footage, sequence). See [Writing assets](/docs/assets).")
    dt#bake Bake
    dd Render an asset once into a file: a frame sequence, one picture, or a WAV, so it costs nothing to draw again.
    dt#caption-lane Caption lane
    dd The band at the bottom of the safe zone reserved for captions.
    dt#clip Clip
    dd A composition: a format, a frame rate, a duration and tracks of items. What you render into a video.
    dt#composition Composition
    dd
      raw md("The data that describes a clip. See [How a clip is built](/docs/compositions).")
    dt#draft Draft render
    dd A quick, smaller, faster-encoded render for checking the cut. Its frames are the same as the full render's, scaled down.
    dt#ducking Ducking
    dd Turning the music down automatically while the narration speaks.
    dt#effect Effect
    dd An asset that processes the pixels of an item, a track or the whole frame: glow, grain, blur, colour grade.
    dt#final-render Final render
    dd A full-size render for publishing, refused while any file in the clip is a placeholder or has no licence, and written with its credits.
    dt#floor Floor
    dd The smallest size a text may be drawn at, as a share of the frame's short side. Text that would need to be smaller fails loudly.
    dt#footage Footage
    dd A video file in the library, placed and trimmed like a picture layer.
    dt#format Format
    dd The shape of the frame: vertical 9:16 (1080 × 1920), horizontal 16:9 (1920 × 1080) or square 1:1 (1080 × 1080).
    dt#item Item
    dd One asset placed on a track, from a start time for a duration, with its parameters and layout.
    dt#keyframe Keyframe
    dd A value of a layout field or a parameter at a moment; the studio eases between keyframes.
    dt#kit Kit
    dd The assets for explainers and marketing: device frames, cursor, spotlight, camera, callouts, arrows, steps, charts, icons, end card.
    dt#lineage Lineage
    dd Which clip produced an asset, what it was forked from, and which later clips reused it.
    dt#loudness LUFS, LU and dBTP
    dd Units of loudness. Streaming platforms aim at about −14 LUFS; LU is a difference in loudness; dBTP is the true peak level.
    dt#marker Marker
    dd A typed note on the timeline: cut, hold, beat, word or note. The checks read them.
    dt#mask Mask
    dd A visual asset, picture, sequence or footage that decides where an item shows.
    dt#mcp MCP
    dd The Model Context Protocol, how Claude Code calls the studio's tools.
    dt#motion Motion
    dd An asset that moves an item without redrawing it: an entrance, an exit, an emphasis or a loop.
    dt#narration Narration
    dd A voice recording with its script and the time of every word.
    dt#override Override
    dd A change to an item's layout, keyframes or parameters for one format only.
    dt#parameter Parameter
    dd A setting of an asset (text, colour, size, speed) with its type, default and limits; the studio builds its controls from them.
    dt#pin Pin
    dd Fix a reference to an exact version (name@3). Saving a clip pins every asset it uses.
    dt#placeholder Placeholder
    dd A stand-in file, marked as such, that a final render refuses.
    dt#playhead Playhead
    dd The current time on the timeline, shown as a vertical line.
    dt#precomp Precomp
    dd An asset that draws several layers, made from layers of a clip with Save as asset.
    dt#preset Preset
    dd An asset that is another asset with chosen parameter values as its defaults.
    dt#proposal Proposal
    dd Claude's answer to a request: a new version, a new asset or clip edits, applied only when you accept it.
    dt#provenance Provenance
    dd Where a file came from: its licence, source, creator and credit.
    dt#remix Remix
    dd A new clip made from an existing one in another format.
    dt#request Request
    dd What you ask the agent in plain words, about an asset, a clip or the library.
    dt#revision Revision
    dd A saved state of a clip. Each save makes a new revision.
    dt#safe-zone Safe zone
    dd The part of the frame no platform button or caption covers. Text belongs inside it.
    dt#sequence Sequence
    dd Frames baked from an asset (PNG with transparency), used as a layer.
    dt#theme Theme
    dd A value asset with a palette and fonts that every asset in a clip can read.
    dt#track Track
    dd A row of the timeline: visual, text or audio. Visual tracks draw from bottom to top.
    dt#transition Transition
    dd An asset that turns one layer into the next.
    dt#version Version
    dd An immutable saved state of an asset (name@1, name@2, …). Editing makes a new version; old ones never change.
